      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A freight elevator can hold a maximum weight of 5,450 pounds during one trip. A 190-pound\nperson needs to deliver several boxes using the freight elevator. Some of these boxes weigh 23\npounds each and the others weigh 60 pounds each. Which inequality represents the possible\ncombinations of the number of 23 -pound boxes, $x$, and the number of 60 -pound boxes, $y$, the\nperson can deliver during one trip if only the person and the boxes are on the freight elevator?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-3e7d0cbb11ba471fa0e0d835a497b138",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q11"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$60 x+23 y \\ge 5$ , 450"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$23 x+60 y \\ge 5$ , 260"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$60 x+23 y \\le 5$ , 450"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$23 x+60 y \\le 5$ , 260"
            }
          ]
        }
